      "writtenOn": "2023-10-26T01:54:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The ectool is more flexible that it can handle files. A simpler way is to give an output file here. And the write command gives an input file. The offset, size, and flags can be handled internally. Multiple host commands may be issued with proper flags. Otherwise, people have to understand the implementation detail to know how to pass a proper flags.\n\nBTW, you may need another host command to know the CBI size so you can check the size first. Maybe call it `EC_CMD_CBI_BIN_INFO`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8774,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 8774,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "d7e2815d06caf1626012d5dea9b38beb5dfe0472",
